# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .gitignore — MDT-Windows-Image-Builder
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# This repository ships scripts, autounattend XML files, and documentation.
# It does not ship Windows ISOs, WIM/ESD/SWM files, VM disk images, or
# captured images — those are multi-GB build artifacts that belong on your
# local machine or a network share, never in Git.
#
# The rules below ignore those artifacts everywhere. If you need to track a
# small binary (a config, a sample, a placeholder), force-add it with
# `git add -f` and explain why in your commit message.
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. WINDOWS INSTALLATION MEDIA AND IMAGES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The output of this repository's workflow. None of these should be
# committed. Store them on your local disk, a network share, or your own
# cloud storage.

# Windows installation images
*.iso
*.img

# Windows Imaging Format files (deployed and capture outputs)
*.wim
*.esd
*.swm

# Full Flash Update (Windows IoT and OEM imaging)
*.ffu

# Windows To Go and similar VHD-based builds
*.vhd
*.vhdx
*.avhdx


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. VIRTUAL MACHINE FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hyper-V, VirtualBox, VMware, and QEMU artifacts created while building or
# testing images. Machine-specific, large, and regenerable.

# Hyper-V
*.vmsn
*.vmsd
*.vmss
*.vmrs
*.bin
*.vsv
*.vhdpmem
Virtual Machines/
Snapshots/

# VirtualBox
*.vbox
*.vbox-prev
*.vdi
*.vbox-extpack

# VMware
*.vmx
*.vmxf
*.vmdk
*.vmem
*.vmsn
*.nvram
*.vmtm
*.vmwarevm/

# QEMU / KVM
*.qcow2
*.qed
*.qcow
*.vmdk


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. UUPDUMP WORKING DIRECTORIES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The UUPDump script produces a working directory with downloaded component
# files, extraction staging, and temporary build output. All of it is
# regenerable from a fresh UUPDump package.

UUPs/
UUPs_*/
UUP/
UUP_*/
*_uupdump*/
aria2c.log
aria2c.session
*.aria2


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. DISM AND SERVICING ARTIFACTS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Staging directories, mount points, and logs created while servicing or
# capturing images.

# Mount points
Mount/
Mounts/
Scratch/
ScratchDir/
DismMount/
DismMounts/
/mnt/
/media/

# Extracted component staging
Extracted/
ExtractedISO/
ISOContent/
ISO-Content/
WinPE/
BootFiles/

# Captured and exported images
Capture/
Captured/
Exported/
Output/
out/
dist/
release/


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. LOGS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sysprep logs, DISM logs, and script logs. These are useful for debugging
# a specific build but should never be committed.

*.log
*.etl
*.evtx

# Sysprep and setup logs
setupact.log
setuperr.log
setupapi.dev.log
setupapi.app.log
sysprep.log
Panther/
Windows/Logs/
DISM/


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. SCRIPTS OUTPUT AND STATE
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# State files, caches, and temporary output written by the repository's
# PowerShell scripts.

# Script state and caches
*.state
*.cache
*.bak
*.tmp
*.temp
*.partial
*.part
*.crdownload

# Script output directories
Temp/
tmp/
cache/
.cache/
LocalState/


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 7. WINDOWS OPERATING SYSTEM JUNK
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Files Windows creates automatically when browsing a folder.

Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk
*.url
*.stackdump
[Dd]esktop.ini


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 8. macOS AND LINUX JUNK
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Contributors using non-Windows editors or running the repo through a
# cross-platform toolchain.

.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
*.swp
*.swo
*~


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 9. EDITOR AND IDE FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json.example
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json.example

.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

.vs/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

*.code-workspace


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 10. POWERSHELL AND SCRIPT ARTIFACTS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

*.ps1xml
PSScriptAnalyzerSettings.psd1.local
TestResults.xml
CodeCoverage.xml
*.Tests.ps1.bak


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 11. SECRETS AND LOCAL CONFIGURATION
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any file that might contain product keys, credentials, or machine-specific
# paths. The repository ships no secrets, and contributors must not
# accidentally commit theirs.

*.personal.*
*.private.*
*.draft.*

# Local overrides of any tracked configuration
*.local.*
!*.local.example
!*.local.template

# Product keys, credentials, and license files
*productkey*
*ProductKey*
*serial*
*license.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
secrets.json
credentials.json


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 12. GIT INTERNAL BACKUPS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.gitattributes.bak
.gitmodules.bak
*.orig.git
*.orig.gitignore


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 13. FINAL OVERRIDES — FILES THAT MUST ALWAYS BE TRACKED
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Re-include files that would otherwise be caught by the broad rules above.

# Keep .gitkeep placeholders so empty directory structures are tracked.
!.gitkeep
!**/.gitkeep

# Documentation assets — screenshots, diagrams, sample output.
!docs/images/**
!docs/examples/**

# Sample configuration and template files that ship with the repository.
!*.example
!*.template
!*.sample

# autounattend XML files — the repository's core artifacts.
!autounattend/**
!autounattend/*.xml

# PowerShell scripts — the repository's automation layer.
!scripts/**
!scripts/*.ps1
!scripts/*.psm1

# Small XML and JSON files used as workflow templates.
!templates/**
!templates/*.xml
!templates/*.json


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# END OF .gitignore
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# If you need to force-add a file that this file ignores, use:
#
#     git add -f <file>
#
# and explain WHY in your commit message and pull request description.
# The reviewer will decide whether the file belongs in the tracked set or
# should be relocated to a regenerable location.
#
# Large binaries (ISOs, WIMs, VM disks) are almost never appropriate for
# this repository. Store them locally or on a share.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
